and on that playlist was

00:01:44.337 --> 00:01:46.473 line:92%
Paris Hilton's "Stars are Blind"

00:01:46.473 --> 00:01:48.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Britney Spears' "Toxic,"
twice.

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:52.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know, but, like, there
was so much of the film --

00:01:52.212 --> 00:01:54.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
the wit of the film
was in the music choices

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the production design
and the costume,

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:57.016 line:92%
and all of that was stuff

00:01:57.016 --> 00:01:58.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
that she presented
along with the script.

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:02.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it was very much she wa
the captain of the ship

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:03.890 line:92%
and we were along for the ride

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:07.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've long been a fan
of Britney Spears' "Toxic.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.929 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will admit
to not being as familiar

00:02:09.929 --> 00:02:12.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Paris Hilton's
work as a singer.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really?
-Yeah, I will admit it.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
But there's
a wonderful sort of --

00:02:16.836 --> 00:02:19.405 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess you guys are in sort o
a pharmacy karaoke scene

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:22.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
with you and Bo Burnham.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:23.543 line:92%
-Are you an actual karaoke fan

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you were very good
in that scene.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:28.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've done --
Yeah, I do a very good

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:31.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
"(Everything I Do)
I Do It For You."

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:35.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, that's my sort of go-to.
And Meat Loaf.

00:02:35.088 --> 00:02:37.090
A little bit of Meat Loaf
on a special occasion.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:38.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I like it.
If you go --

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:40.493
That's the thing about karaoke
If you're gonna get your sho

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:41.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then wait
for everybody else,

00:02:41.528 --> 00:02:44.030
you got to do one of those
eight-minute Meat Loaf songs

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.798 line:92%
just get your time up onstage.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.467 line:92%
-You've got to do the duet

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:51.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
Play the woman, the dude,
you know, really get into it

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
-i mean, that really
speaks to ego

00:02:53.273 --> 00:02:55.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you won't let someone els
come out with you

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:57.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
and split the parts up.
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:57.744 --> 00:03:00.914 line:92%
-No. The only one I ever do.

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:03.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
Those two are my numbers.
-Yeah, I agree.

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:05.552
I think people should drill down
on one or two they're good at.

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:08.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nobody wants to see somebody d
a giant catalog of songs.

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:13.993 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want to be careful talking
too much about this film,

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:15.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I would hate
to give it away,

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:21.834
because for as much as it seem
like it was in such safe hands

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
insofar as what it
was trying to do,

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:26.773
there were so many turns that
did not see coming at all.

00:03:26.773 --> 00:03:28.575 size:78% position:39%
And there were times
where I thought, "Oh,

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:31.711
this would be a film
that would be a great experience

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:34.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
to see in a theater
with other people

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:37.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
having these same realizations
at the same time.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:39.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you think that, ever?
-Yeah.

00:03:39.285 --> 00:03:42.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, we were lucky enough
that we had that.

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:45.725
We had a sort of first screening
at Sundance,

00:03:45.725 --> 00:03:49.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we got to sort of sit
amongst an audience and feel..

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:52.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I'm so used
to being in sort of dramas

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:56.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
where the best you can hope fo
is a pin-drop silence.

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:58.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
You just want --
you want nothing.

00:03:58.404 --> 00:03:59.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
And with
"Promising Young Woman,"

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:01.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
we were getting gasps
and we were getting laughter

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:03.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we were getting people
like, yelling.

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:07.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was so exciting.
So, it's definitely a sham

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:09.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
that more people won't see i
in the cinema,

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:11.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I think it's also
one of those great things

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
about independent film,
when it gets --

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:16.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
sort of when people
take notice of it,

00:04:16.022 --> 00:04:17.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
then we get
such a bigger audience,

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.626 size:81% position:41%
and maybe more people
will watch it at home.

00:04:19.626 --> 00:04:20.760 align:start size:94% position:6%
So who knows?
-Is it true

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:23.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
that there was a fight,
an actual fight, broke out

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:25.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
at one of
the Sundance screenings?

00:04:25.498 --> 00:04:26.566 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:28.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was actually --
